{"type": "thinking", "text": "No error shown for existing name (no \"already exists\" message). SAVE enabled. Tap SAVE to see what happens. This is a potential bug if it overwrites keep.jpg instead of error. But careful: testing this could destroy keep.jpg. Hmm, \"Do not change data outside what testing requires.\" Renaming to existing file may replace it. Risky. Let me think: the spec asks to test renaming; conflict handling is relevant. But if the app overwrites keep.jpg, I lose the test data. I could instead test conflict with a name that is less critical... still any existing file. Alternatively, create a temp file? Not allowed outside testing? Creating then deleting is probably fine, but let's not.\n\nActually a rename collision test is important. Perhaps the app shows a confirmation dialog \"keep.jpg already exists. Overwrite?\" Let me tap SAVE and see. If it overwrites, I can restore by renaming to keep.jpg... wait keep.jpg and notes2.txt have different content sizes (21kB vs 15B) so overwriting keep.jpg with notes2.txt would destroy photo data. Not good.\n\nLet me instead cancel and test collision in the copy/paste flow (which is the changed feature and safer since copy doesn't destroy source; paste conflict). For rename collision, skip destructive test.\n\nActually careful: could test rename to a name of a file we can recover, e.g., rename notes2.txt to report+final.txt — that would overwrite report+final.txt (13B). Still destructive.\n\nAlternative: Create a temporary test folder/file? \"Do not change data outside what testing requires\" — creating a test file is arguably within testing. But then cleanup. Hmm.\n\nLet's just cancel and not test rename collision destructively. Maybe rename's error handling appears when Save is tapped. It could show a dialog. Let's tap SAVE and observe quickly; if it's a dialog, cancel.\n\nActually if Save immediately renames with overwrite, we'd lose data. Risk. But maybe replacment just deletes keep.jpg and renames notes2.txt. That would be bad.\n\nHmm, but the changed build says nothing about rename conflicts. The critical rename change is prefill. I've verified. Let's cancel and rename back to notes.txt.\n\nCancel this dialog."}
