at if a bookmark's target folder is renamed, the entry should show the current name? No — bookmarks store a title; renaming the target doesn't rename the bookmark necessarily. In many file managers, bookmarks keep the stored name. So not a bug.\n\nLet me click the drawer bookmark \"Alpha\" (element 35 merged but tap coordinates 399,788) and see where it goes. It should open /AndroidQA/Amaze/Alpha (now nonexistent). The app may open a path that doesn't exist (empty). That's acceptable? Or maybe it fails. Let's test as part of bookmark behavior (stale path). Hmm, but it's not necessarily part of changed build.\n\nActually, the more important test for \"read afresh each time the drawer opens\": After adding a bookmark (e.g., Beta), without restarting, opening drawer should show it. We saw Alpha appear immediately after adding. That works.\n\nAnother test: delete a bookmarked folder -> open drawer -> does the bookmark entry persist (stale) or disappear? Hmm. The change may be about the drawer reading the bookmarks database fresh, so newly added/removed bookmarks reflect. We saw add reflects.\n\nLet me check draw \"add bookmark\" updates: add Beta bookmark, open drawer (closes then reopens), see Beta appears. Then remove bookmark via drawer's pencil/edit icon? Let's explore the pencil icon for the Alpha bookmark (element 36 imageButton at 724,788). Tapping might open an edit dialog with \"Delete\" option. Let's test later.\n\nFirst check navigation from bookmark. But tapping a stale path might cause an error screen; could be a bug but caused by our rename. Better: rename AlphaQA back to Alpha first, then test bookmark navigation and removal. But before that, note the stale title - we can test if the drawer entry shows updated label after rename back? It'd still be Alpha anyway.\n\nActually, let's test what happens tapping the bookmark while its target is missing — the changed \"read afresh\" might reveal something: maybe app shows a toast \"Folder not found\" or opens ro