ndroidQA -> Amaze. List showed Alpha, Beta (2 folders).\n4. Opened context menu, tapped \"Add to Bookmarks\" (not rename) — this added Alpha again maybe duplicates (didn't).\n5. Opened drawer, saw Alpha bookmark still.\n6. Closed drawer.\n7. Context menu -> Rename -> renamed Alpha -> AlphaQA. Observed list: AlphaQA, Beta (2 folders).\n8. Opened drawer; Alpha entry stale.\n9. Tapped drawer Alpha -> navigated to /.../Alpha (missing), showing 0/0 No Files.\n10. Pressed back -> list shows Alpha (7:05), AlphaQA, Beta (3 folders).\n\nSo yes, step 9 created the empty Alpha directory. That's a bug: opening a bookmark to a missing folder silently creates the folder. Or maybe the app's path view always calls mkdirs? Hmm.\n\nBut wait, maybe the folder \"Alpha\" at 7:05 is not empty but is the *file picker's* created directory. Let me inspect: open Alpha and check contents."}
