{"type": "thinking", "text": "Data restored (photo.jpg). Also note the file sort: keep, notes, photo, report — name ordering? Actually current sort should be Name ascending (we reset earlier), so keep, notes, photo, report. Yes correct. Good.\n\nNow, the empty-folder-creation bug: Let's verify once more methodically and then report. Steps:\n1. Rename Alpha -> AlphaQA.\n2. Open drawer (bookmark Alpha is stale).\n3. Tap bookmark Alpha → view shows /.../Alpha with \"0 folders and 0 files\"/\"No Files\".\n4. Press back → list now includes a new empty \"Alpha\" folder (created just now, timestamp 7:0x).\nExpected: opening a bookmark to a missing folder should show error/empty without creating the folder on disk (or the bookmark should update to the renamed folder).\nObserved: new empty folder Alpha created.\n\nBut is this within \"changed in this build\" bookmarks? The changed note says \"bookmark entries are now read afresh each time the drawer opens.\" Maybe the bug they introduced is related: bookmark path not refreshed -> clicking stale path creates folder. Hmm.\n\nActually, wait. Maybe the drawer bookmark's *target path* was ALSO updated to the new folder (AlphaQA) by \"read afresh\", but the displayed title stayed Alpha? When I tapped the bookmark, we landed at /.../Alpha, not AlphaQA. So path unchanged.\n\nLet me test the behavior again cleanly. Important: after we renamed back, the bookmark points to Alpha valid. To repro:\n- Rename Alpha -> AlphaQA.\n- Open drawer; tap bookmark row at y≈788 (second row under Internal Storage).\n- Observe path. Then back; observe whether Alpha recreated.\nLet me do it.\n\nActually, maybe the empty folder was created not by bookmark navigation but by pressing \"Rename\" with AlphaQA->Alpha? No, the Alpha at 7:05 appeared right after the bookmark tap (before rename back). And after rename, the folder mtime would be 6:58 from original. The new Alpha had 7:05 and was empty, proving creation.\n\nAlternatively, could the app have created Alpha when the context menu \"Add to Bookmarks\" was tapped? That was earlier (7:04-ish). The Alpha at 7:05 appeared after bookmark tap at 7:05. Hmm, \"Add to Bookmarks\" shouldn't create folders.\n\nOK reproduce now. Rename Alpha -> AlphaQA. Then open drawer and click the bookmark.\n\nWait, is bookmark Alpha still in the drawer after rename? Yes, title Alpha. Let's do."}
