{"type": "thinking", "text": "Reproduced! A new empty \"Alpha\" folder (7:07 AM) appeared after opening the stale bookmark, while AlphaQA (6:58) is the real folder. This is a bug: navigating to a missing bookmark target creates the missing directory. But is it Amaze's behavior to create folders when opening a path? It seems the file manager does `mkdirs()` maybe for bookmark navigation. That's data-changing; a bug worth reporting in bookmarks area. But is it caused by the bookmark being stale (renamed folder)? Maybe more general: any bookmark to a non-existent path creates it. That's a real defect.\n\nHowever, the more direct \"changed\" behavior is bookmark entries read afresh each time drawer opens. Hmm, the stale entry itself: after renaming the target folder, the drawer bookmark still shows old name and stale path. Is that a bug? If bookmarks are read afresh from the DB, the title is stored, so it stays. The change note might imply that when a bookmark is *removed/added*, drawer reflects it. We should test that.\n\nBut this empty folder creation is a strong, confirmed bug. Let me clean up first: delete new empty Alpha, rename AlphaQA back to Alpha. Then file report.\n\nActually let me first record exact data: path /storage/emulated/0/AndroidQA/Amaze/Alpha shows \"0 folders and 0 files\" and \"No Files\"; after back the list says \"3 folders and 4 files\" with Alpha (7:07 AM) and AlphaQA (6:58). Good.\n\nCleanup: currently in Amaze. Delete Alpha (element 8, 0 folders). Then rename AlphaQA back.\n\nLet me delete Alpha."}
