ed \"Add to Bookmarks\" for the second time — no.\n\nHmm, what about \"Open in Terminal\"? No.\n\nWhat if the app creates the folder when the bookmark is *added* to store its path? No, path existed.\n\nWhat if the file manager's \"No Files\" view for a missing path auto-mkdirs? That's what I suspect; but developer couldn't reproduce. Maybe because the bookmark's stored path got updated to \"AlphaQA\" when reopened in their test (read afresh), so tapping opens the existing folder, no creation. In our case, the drawer bookmark entry stayed stale \"Alpha\" because... hmm, actually maybe the \"read afresh\" fix works: when the drawer is opened, it reads bookmark entries from DB. The DB entry still has title/path Alpha (we added it before rename). It doesn't auto-update. So tapping opens missing path → app creates folder? Maybe the creation is from the *empty view's* code which calls `mkdirs`? Unclear.\n\nAnyway, developer couldn't reproduce; likely they tested differently (maybe they didn't rename the target; or they didn't look for the created folder). I should not dwell. I now have two unconfirmed reports. Perhaps my reports are being rejected because the behavior is considered expected or the steps lack something.\n\nLet me test the \"bookmarks read afresh\" behavior directly as intended:\n- Remove a bookmark while the app is running (via drawer pencil/edit icon) → close & reopen drawer → entry should be gone.\n- Add bookmark to Beta via context menu → open drawer → Beta appears immediately.\nThis is likely the changed feature. If broken, that's the bug to report.\n\nFirst restore data: rename AlphaQA back to Alpha. Also the stale \"Alpha\" bookmark will then be valid. Then test removing bookmark.\n\nLet's close drawer (back), rename AlphaQA -> Alpha."}
