{"type": "thinking", "text": "Beta bookmark deleted immediately. Drawer back to defaults. Good.\n\nNow, back to the unconfirmed bugs. Maybe I should re-examine the grid loss more carefully to find a *different* actual bug. Wait, maybe the grid/list toggle behavior is: \"Grid View\" option in the overflow toggles between grid and list; but after rotation, the app re-reads the preference from SharedPreferences. Perhaps the preference is only written on `onPause`, which doesn't happen on rotation? Hmm, rotation calls onPause, so it should save. Unless the debug build's config changes no... Hmm.\n\nMaybe the developer couldn't reproduce because they tested \"Grid View\" in the *drawer*? Hmm.\n\nLet me consider that the device harness might be doing something like resetting app state on rotation? But sort persisted, so no.\n\nCould the \"Grid View\" menu item actually be \"switch to grid for this session only\"? In Amaze, the overflow has \"Grid View\" checkbox in older versions; toggling changes mode and persists via preference. Normally it persists across restart. If this build has a bug where it doesn't persist, restarting the app (open_app) would also reset to list. Let's test: currently list. Select grid, then press HOME, reopen app (open_app), check grid. If grid reset, that confirms grid isn't persisted at all. That's a more general and easier-to-reproduce bug (\"Grid View selection not persisted\"). Maybe the developer's repro attempts didn't include rotation but would include app restart.\n\nLet me test. Close drawer (back). Then tap Grid View, then HOME, then open_app, observe."}
