{"type": "thinking", "text": "Good, back in list (because Beta grid? Wait it shows list; earlier Beta was grid, now Amaze shows list. Hmm, because I set grid in Beta, and returning to Amaze shows list? Wait, we set Grid View in Beta at 7:?? and the app was grid; then HOME/open_app showed Beta grid; then I pressed BACK to Amaze, and now Amaze shows LIST. So grid mode did NOT apply to Amaze, while earlier in portrait it did (when we set grid at Amaze, Alpha was grid). Interesting: the grid setting may be per-folder? Hmm, when we set Grid View in Beta, only Beta changed; Amaze stayed list. Earlier when we set grid at Amaze, Alpha showed grid when opened. So maybe grid view is per-folder preference, stored per path. That's plausible: \"Only this folder\" concept? Hmm, Amaze has a per-folder view setting? It could save per-directory display mode. Actually maybe not; earlier when we set grid at Amaze, then navigated into Alpha and it was grid, suggesting global. But then Beta grid not propagating to Amaze suggests per-folder.\n\nWait, maybe the reason Amaze is list: When we set grid in Beta, then pressed HOME and open_app (grid persisted), then BACK to Amaze — Amaze was previously list because... hmm, we had set grid in Beta only. So per-folder makes sense: grid setting applies to Beta only.\n\nBut earlier: we set grid at Amaze (tapping Grid View in Amaze), then opened Alpha (grid), then back to Amaze (grid). That's consistent with global too, but also with \"global default for new folders\"? Hmm.\n\nActually maybe view mode is stored per-folder in a map. Amaze = grid? No wait, after setting grid at Amaze, Amaze was grid, Alpha grid (because new folder inherits global? or because Alpha had no per-folder setting). Then later when we set grid in Beta while Beta list... Hmm.\n\nThere might be a per-folder \"grid\" preference keyed by path. If so, rotation behavior: rotating resets to *global/default* because it reads a different key? Hmm, hmm.\n\nWait, this could explain the